{#- A folded option's description: a directed word with its direction
    (`reconcile.build_items`, one option of the `decision` choice per way the
    word may run, its id `reconcile.folded(word, frm, to)`). Vars: word
    ("duplicate" | "continuation" | "subthread" | "pays_off"), frm and to
    (the letters "A" | "B" it runs from and to). The retired prompt's
    direction rules, one clause per word (`verify_templates.py`'s
    RECONCILE_REWORDED). The records' lines are already in the item's
    context, so the description only names them by letter (M1). -#}
{%- if word == "duplicate" -%}
the same record: fold record {{ frm }} away into record {{ to }}, the one to keep
{%- elif word == "continuation" -%}
record {{ frm }} continues record {{ to }}
{%- elif word == "subthread" -%}
record {{ frm }} is a subthread of record {{ to }}
{%- elif word == "pays_off" -%}
record {{ frm }}, the plot thread, pays off record {{ to }}, the commitment
{%- endif -%}
